        "id": 1351609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T17:03:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just in case, is `BluetoothManager` ever held in any static field in framework code? Asking just to make sure we aren\u0027t introducing a memory leak.",
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cae515a2_29bc2853",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T17:13:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Holding a context or an AttributionSource should be the same level of memory leak4",
      "parentUuid": "3ad63ba4_cc45cb87",
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad51ef0e_dc03a0d9",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1351609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T17:34:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Holding a `Context` that is actually an `Activity` in a static field would leak that `Activity` - I don\u0027t think that can happen with holding an `AttributionSource` in a static field.",
      "parentUuid": "cae515a2_29bc2853",
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c6bb7f2_126e9aa7",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T17:49:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh I see.\n\nI believe there is no such thin. The BluetoothManager is create as a context aware service [here](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothFrameworkInitializer.java;l\u003d99;drc\u003d1c07fc7429516c128c0725796c8db4c582b2b8cb), and the way this is retrieve is by doing:\n\n`context.getSystemService(BluetoothManager.class)`",
      "parentUuid": "ad51ef0e_dc03a0d9",
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa3c854c_0d3fc8d3",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1651020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T12:48:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we create context.createDeviceContext(DEVICE_ID_DEFAULT).getAttributionSource() here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82375685_ae377e70",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T16:53:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand what this will do.\nAlso…\nBy looking at the usage, `createDeviceContext` is only used in `Activity.java`, in `VirtualDeviceInternal.java`, in the PermissionManagerService.\nEverything else is test.\n\nThis is not a very spread usage and make me worries that this is not really intended for here.\nBluetooth doesn\u0027t care about what device it is running on and only use the one given at construction. I believe that if an app knows what it is doing, they can do the `createDeviceContext` on their own, before calling getSystemService on it ?",
      "parentUuid": "aa3c854c_0d3fc8d3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed4cecad_3cf5e8f6",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1351609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T17:03:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we let `BluetoothAdapter` take `Context` so that it won\u0027t have an outdated `AttributionSource` either?",
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4aa5f6c5_38a4d38c",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T17:13:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is currently not possible because robolectric depends on the AttributionSource constructor.\nI tried to make this modification a few weeks earlier and it break a few tests (I opened b/343739429 for that)\n\nEven when keeping the old constructor to take an optional context, the reflexion made by robolectric doesn\u0027t catch the correct constructor.\n\nAlso, the BluetoothAdapter can be retrieve from the deprecated static method getDefaultAdapter and this does not require a context in argument.",
      "parentUuid": "ed4cecad_3cf5e8f6",
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e649a89a_74e5f97a",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1351609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T17:32:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack, I don\u0027t think this need to block the submission of the current CL.\n\n@marvinramin@google.com wdyt?",
      "parentUuid": "4aa5f6c5_38a4d38c",
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65e6cc96_4416ab3a",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1651020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T18:08:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed.",
      "parentUuid": "e649a89a_74e5f97a",
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4f10024_f1afcefd",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1651020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T18:08:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would effectively modify/overwrite the deviceID of the device the calling app is running on (e.g. on the phone vs streamed to a chromebook). It\u0027s best if we don\u0027t overwrite it and honor the context that was passed in. In case we need further workarounds we can consider createDeviceContext() which we use both inside and outside the framework (my team owns this API).",
      "parentUuid": "82375685_ae377e70",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "a266e91fd39788c27a48fb046f19cb6389a2a91c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
